# L §7.6 item 1, §8.3 item 9 (tally 2.1.6, issue #89): a move's day that load sees, on end_of(y) for the key 9999 of
# the built-in years, is the end of time, no day: LOAD-LIMIT with the move and its key. tally 2.1.5's refcore refused
# the model REFCORE-NOT-YET (its run lies in 9999).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 9999-12-31
  start 9999-01-01
  end 9999-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place other: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN

move fee[y in years]: transfers
  on end_of(y)
  leg cash from konto to landlord amount amt

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 9999-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "plan"

ask f: flows(konto, 9999)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LIMIT move fee[9999] on end_of(y): a day passes 9999-12-31 (m.tally:14)
